[00:01.54] High class Slim came floatin' in
[00:05.02] Down from the county line
[00:39.24] Just gettin' right on Saturday night
[00:43.46] Ridin' with some friends of mine
[00:46.86] They invited me just to come and see
[00:51.26] Just what was on their minds
[00:54.88] And then I took my first long look
[00:58.32] At the Master of Sparks on high
[01:02.80] In the back of Jimmy's Mack
[01:06.80] Stood a round steel cage
[01:09.98] Welded into shape by Slim
[01:14.16] Made out of sucker gauge
[01:17.90] How fine, they cried, now with you inside
[01:22.06] Strapped in there safe and sound
[01:25.20] I thought, my-o-my, how the sparks will fly
[01:29.42] If that thing ever hit the ground
[01:33.36] Slim was so pleased when I had eased
[01:37.00] Into his trap of death
[01:40.38] He had slammed the door but I said no more
[01:44.26] And I thought I'd breathed my last breath
[01:48.20] We was out in the sticks down Highway Six
[01:51.92] And the crowd was just about right
[01:55.92] The speed was too, so out I flew
[01:59.48] Like a stick of rollin' dynamite
[02:50.92] When I hit the ground you could hear the sound
[02:54.80] And see the sparks a country mile
[02:58.66] End over end I began to spin
[03:01.84] But the ball started runnin' wild
[03:05.80] But it was too late as I met my fate
[03:09.64] And the ball started gettin' hot
[03:13.16] But through the sparks and the flame I knew that the claim
[03:17.04] Of the Master of Sparks was gone
